// trajectory_carpet.mat — VM-077. output_trajectory_carpet's per-vertex
// color IS the signal (the producer's own baked velocity gradient,
// STANDING directive 2026-09-09) -- UNLIT for the same reason
// point_cloud.mat is: PBR shading would add a light-direction term nobody
// asked for, and `CarpetVertex` (position + packed rgba, no tangent frame)
// couldn't feed one anyway.
//
// `requires : [ color ]`: the per-vertex rgba8 trajectory_carpet.cpp's
// CarpetVertex carries, baked ONCE by the node-side adapter (from the
// marker's own colors[]) and never re-baked.
//
// OPAQUE (flicker root-cause fix, 2026-09-10): this was `blending : fade`
// with a staleness `alpha` uniform -- but that parked the velocity ribbon
// PERMANENTLY in Filament's blended queue (per-renderable sort, no depth
// writes), where it and the also-blended BEHAVIOR ribbon on the same spine
// overpainted each other by rebuild order -- the live binary teal flicker
// (see ribbon_emissive.mat's own 2026-09-10 note and test_ribbon_dropout
// .cpp's repro). Opaque writes depth, so the z-stagger (velocity 0.052
// below BEHAVIOR 0.058, above LOCAL 0.046) decides per-pixel. Staleness
// now fades via an instance swap to trajectory_carpet_faded.mat (the fade
// twin that keeps this shader plus the alpha uniform) -- the same swap
// mechanism ribbon.cpp uses; clay_translucent.mat can't serve here because
// it's LIT (CarpetVertex has no tangent frame) and has no vertex color.
material {
    name : trajectory_carpet,
    shadingModel : unlit,
    requires : [ color ]
}
fragment {
    void material(inout MaterialInputs material) {
        prepareMaterial(material);
        material.baseColor.rgb = getColor().rgb;
        material.baseColor.a = 1.0;
    }
}
